cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this lab in a write-up or talk, cite it as below."
title: "php2shell-lab: differential reproduction of the PHP php2shell fixes (CVE-2026-109618 / CVE-2026-109619)"
abstract: >-
  A differential harness that runs the same two-request trigger against PHP
  8.4.26 (vulnerable) and PHP 8.4.27 (fixed), both built from source with
  AddressSanitizer. It reproduces the pre-RINIT state-corruption bug fixed by
  PHP commit 506e87fa and documents what the circulating public PoCs actually
  do. It does not demonstrate remote code execution.
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-21
license: MIT
type: software
url: "https://github.com/allureluoli/php2shell-lab"
keywords:
  - php
  - php2shell
  - CVE-2026-109618
  - CVE-2026-109619
  - session-upload-progress
  - addresssanitizer
  - vulnerability-reproduction
authors:
